<http://data.silknow.org/object/69cdcb24-6fa7-3e96-8942-a81a80c8c140/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nMary Queen of Scots (1542-1587)<br>\nMary Queen of Scots' troubled reign in Scotland ended in 1568 when the Scottish Lords forced her to flee across the border into England. As Elizabeth's cousin Mary had long claimed the English throne, leading Elizabeth to see Mary as a threat and place her in the custody of the Earl of Shrewsbury. Mary was held captive in various English country houses for 19 years. She was finally executed in 1587.<br><br>\n\nMary Queen of Scots (1542-1587) embroidered these panels with Elizabeth Talbot, Countess of Shrewsbury (Bess of Hardwick) and ladies of the household, during her imprisonment. Mary may have intended the large central panel as a cushion for Philip Howard, Earl of Arundel (1557-1595), an English Catholic courtier imprisoned in London by Elizabeth I. Mary's emblem of the marigold turning towards the sun (lower right) has been combined with various coats of arms and emblems representing courage in adversity.  Many other panels from the same group are now at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/69cdcb24-6fa7-3e96-8942-a81a80c8c140> .

<http://data.silknow.org/vam>
        ecrm:P106_is_composed_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b1276ab8-4c39-3d27-be94-b0e7432dcd27> .

<http://data.silknow.org/event/d3568557-c68e-36a5-b647-8122b75888f1>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Made by Mary Queen of Scots, Elizabeth, Countess of Shrewsbury and members of her household. Probably made in Sheffield Castle where Mary was imprisoned. The Oxburgh Hangings. Embroidered hanging from Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk. Originally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/d858d816-5ef4-3380-8e9e-1aff3f2527db> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Presented by Art Fund" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/69cdcb24-6fa7-3e96-8942-a81a80c8c140> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Made by Mary Queen of Scots, Elizabeth, Countess of Shrewsbury and members of her household. Probably made in Sheffield Castle where Mary was imprisoned. The Oxburgh Hangings. Embroidered hanging from Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk. Originally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels."@en .

